00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:01.860
Episode 32 
The Traitor

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:04.250
So this is Earth.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.480
So blue, so beautiful... {how blue, how beautiful}

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.670
Message from codename Maria:

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:13.110
"I've found a castle in the jungle." End of message.

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:16.170
Now we can finally mobilize the fleet.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:20.320
It took a long time to determine the coordinates.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.590
Zeheart's spies aren't what they used to be. {the quality of the spies in Zeheart's squadron has fallen}

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:29.740
I would have expected them to work harder, 
considering their unit reports directly to Lord Ezelcant.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.060
Attention, all ships.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.850
We will now begin our landing operation.

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:40.190
Our target is the Federation's South American base, Rostroulan.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:50.160
Okay, break time.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.670
Yeah!

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.130
Well done, everyone.

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.440
Here, have some lunch.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:55.250
Here!

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:58.080
Hey, thanks.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.710
You just ate, Taku!

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:03.750
Good work, Wootbit.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.640
Thank you.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:11.680
By single-seater, do you mean the AGE-3 will have just one pilot?

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.980
Can I do it by myself?

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.600
It'll be fine. Have some confidence.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:20.000
Former Commander Asuno specifically requested this modification.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:21.960
He did?

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:25.430
It means he's acknowledged that you'll be okay on your own.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:30.890
Anyway, I've been so busy lately.

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:32.580
Help me out, man!

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:37.310
I'd love to, but is there anything I can actually do?

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:40.060
What are you saying? You're part of the Asuno family!

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:43.340
I've never been taught any maintenance stuff.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:47.850
But you're the grandson of Flit Asuno, who made the Gundam.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:48.640
What a waste!

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.550
My grandpa taught me a lot.

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:56.390
But all we had at our place were worker machines.

00:04:56.390 --> 00:05:00.270
I never dreamed I'd get to touch a mobile suit.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:04.460
My mom was a mobile suit pilot,

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:08.070
but she'd {angrily told me, etc, this is awkward}scold me{any butt slapping?} whenever I tinkered with 
machines and told me to go read a book instead.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:12.460
She was against me being on the Diva to the bitter end.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.220
My mom would always just watch me and laugh.

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:18.170
I don't think I've ever seen her mad.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:21.940
I'd love to have that kind of family.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:26.070
Taku, enough already!

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:28.410
But it looks yummy!

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:31.710
No, no! This is mine!

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:35.320
Taku, stop bothering them.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:36.200
Yeah!

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:37.890
Wendy...

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:39.100
Still working hard, I see.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.600
Everybody has to stay onboard till we reach the base.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.530
Somebody's gotta look after you guys.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:45.560
Kio!

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:49.440
You haven't had your medical check yet.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:52.620
If you don't take it, they won't let you in the Gundam.

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:54.040
Right.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:58.370
If you don't show, I'll tell Ms. Romary.{SERIOUSLY, why didn't anyone fix this last week? WHO CALLS THEIR OWN SISTER-IN-LAW MS.???}{seriously thinking to drop Ms.}

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:03.910
Kio, did you get in touch with your mom?

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:05.010
I'll do it later.

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.880
I'm sure she's worried.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:11.220
Yeah, I know that, but...

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:14.390
Kio, be more thoughtful towards your family.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:16.810
M-Ms. Shanalua!

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.110
Don't say you'll do it later.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:20.730
Contact them right now.

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:22.400
Yes, ma'am!

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:26.150
That's what I like to hear.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:29.070
Talk to her while you still can.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.550
Helm, all normal.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:42.220
Maintaining current course and speed.

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:45.700
We'll reach Rostroulan in half a day, all according to schedule.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.020
Where's the captain?

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:48.800
Meeting with the former Commander.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:51.220
Jeez...

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:53.650
Another lecture?

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:57.870
An indecisive captain isn't a captain at all. {a captain without decisiveness is absurd}

00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:01.500
Delaying orders will only result in more people dying.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:02.490
Yes, sir.

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:06.050
Take some pride in the fact that you've been given a ship.

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:10.900
If nothing else, I believe you have the makings of a captain.

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:18.440
But when I think that the lives of soldiers hinge on my decision...

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:19.330
I just...

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:24.950
I'm going to advise you for a little while.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:29.010
First, let's work on that indecisive attitude again.

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:31.980
I'm very sorry.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:33.550
Excuse me.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:36.200
Sergeant Major Wong.{Hm...doesn't look Chinese to me}

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:40.040
I'd like to report something to the captain.

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:42.710
Go on.

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:00.620
An info leak? {surely htere is a better way to say this in english}

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:02.020
Yes.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:05.650
The signal corps' report {signal corps sound retared. it's literally "communication sqad" but there has to be a miltiary term for that}{yeah, the term is "signal corps"} has arrived from central command.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:12.050
They've found out that encrypted, compressed data is being sent out regularly via the crew's network.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:15.360
The leak appears to be an innocuous message to a family member,

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:18.720
but it's automatically being sent somewhere else as well.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:20.390
Somewhere else?

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:23.940
To a facility believed to be connected to the Vagans.

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:29.850
Do we know the sender?

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:30.690
Yes.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:33.130
It's Lieutenant Shanalua Mullen.{Why are ranks abbreviated sometimes and written in full others, like with Wong?}{agreed, lets make it consistent}

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:54.170
What is it?

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:56.840
A large-scale landing operation by the Vagans!

00:08:56.840 --> 00:09:00.560
It looks like Rostroulan has entered combat status.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:01.760
But that's...

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:06.300
Even when the Vagans staged their mass uprising, they couldn't find it!

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:08.940
Could this be...

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:11.360
They've determined its location.

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:13.220
Thanks to the spy.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.460
All ships have completed their descent.

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:42.080
Report deployment status of mobile suit teams.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:45.640
All landing teams, commence attack 
according to the operation plans.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:48.900
Update all information pertaining to 
enemy defenses on the shared database.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.410
The mobile suit deployment is too slow!

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:53.750
We'll lose the advantage of a preemptive attack!

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:54.320
Yes, sir!

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:57.620
Well now, the table's been set.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:00.990
Let's see what Lord Ezelcant's personal team can do.

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.900
Zeheart.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:08.960
<i>Mobile suits have now been loaded with plasma particle bombs.{Hey, it's that VA who always plays the goofball roles}</i>

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:09.830
Okay.

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:16.170
After we land, we'll join up with the vanguard forces.

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:19.360
<i>Darest team, target the outer energy plants.</i>

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:21.520
<i>Leil team, follow me.</i>

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.600
<i>Roger.</i>

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:27.180
Zeheart Galette, Wrozzo. Heading out.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:35.820
What?

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:37.740
Inspect Shanalua's mobile suit?

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:39.320
What do you—

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.660
<i>There's no time to explain!</i>

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:44.550
The area around Rostroulan is a wetland,

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:45.700
so you should stay in Fortress form.

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:49.400
You can pilot it basically the same way as in the desert.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:50.690
Got it.

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:52.540
I know you can do it!

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.470
Yeah. Thanks, Wootbit.

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:07.600
<i>What's going on, Shanalua?</i>

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:08.910
<i>We aren't launching yet!</i>

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:13.020
Don't let that Clanche launch!

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.240
Restrain it!

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.130
What's going on, Derek?

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:20.950
<i>Shanalua was a spy!</i>

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:24.030
Ms. Shanalua{the spy who almost-shagged-me}?

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:26.400
What does he mean?

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:28.070
<i>You're not a spy, are you?</i>

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:36.090
Ms. Shanalua!

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:09.790
23rd Squadron, fall back to secondary defense base!

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:13.120
The enemy has deployed a large number of new ground-based weapon models!

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:16.130
Stop the ground-based enemies with the mobile suits!

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.880
Anti-air units, focus your attacks on the ships!

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:22.170
The Diva has entered the combat zone from the northwest.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:24.890
Its mobile suits are on standby.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.800
Impressive, Commander Asuno.

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:29.850
As always, you know just {how to give me a boner, seriously i have a massive man crush on you old geezer i even grew this stache because i worship you}{wat}when you're needed.

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:32.980
Have the Diva join the battle formation.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.480
Tell them to handle the western coastal area!

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.740
Seric Abis, Clanche Custom, heading out!

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:48.160
Derek Jacklow, Clanche, heading out!

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:00.670
I'm going after Ms. Shanalua.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:04.340
<i>Defending Rostroulan is more important than the spy right now!</i>

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:05.590
Why?

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:07.260
We don't know that she's a spy yet.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:10.930
<i>Shanalua Mullen launched when she was told to stay put.</i>

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:13.520
<i>That's clear proof she's a spy.{lolololo makes it sound like anyone who launches without permission is a spy. clearly should be something like, launching without permission was the nail in the coffin in terms of evidence}{it's what he says, however retarded it may be}{amuro was zeon's greatest spy}</i>

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.480
Let the traitor go.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:19.440
Our priority is to defend the base.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.440
Traitor...

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:38.380
Kio Asuno. Gundam AGE-3 Fortress.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.540
Heading out.

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:45.800
Kio, where are you going?

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:50.100
I'm sorry, Grandpa.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.260
I just can't let her go.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:54.680
<i>I want to know the truth.</i>

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:54.910
Where am I supposed to run?

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:31.950
Ms. Shanalua...

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:33.030
An enemy?

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:01.230
A friendly marker?{yeah but is this how military would say it}{A marker indicating an ally more likely}

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.060
Ms. Shanalua?

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:27.380
<i>Ms. Shanalua!</i>

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.050
Ms. Shanalua!

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:42.850
Why, Ms. Shanalua?

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:45.480
<i>Why did you become a Vagan spy?</i>

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:52.490
I wanted my sister to get proper medical treatment.

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:55.950
I needed money.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:14.630
My sister is very sick.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:18.100
Without continual treatment, she might die.

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:22.310
I didn't have a choice!

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:25.980
I didn't want to lose the only family I have.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:32.230
Let's go back.

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:35.700
I thought of you as a big sister.{friend zoned}

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:37.910
I'd hate it if I couldn't see you anymore.

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.160
What happens if I go back?

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:42.830
I'm an enemy spy.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:50.500
The Gundam?

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.760
You guys go on to the assigned point.

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:56.680
I'm going to take out the Gundam.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:57.510
Yes, sir.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:02.720
<i>I'll do anything I can!</i>

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:03.930
<i>So...</i>

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:07.390
<i>Kio... war isn't that nice.</i>

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:10.610
<i>If you're piloting that thing...</i>

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:13.320
<i>You'd better have what it takes to do it right.</i>

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:17.150
What it takes...?

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:23.580
Ms. Shanalua!

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:29.540
If I go back to the Diva with you, I'll be executed as a spy.

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:32.250
I can't let myself die now.

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:35.840
I have to live, for my sister's sake!

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:36.920
I must!

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:41.140
I'll explain it to Grandpa!

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:42.850
If I ask him, I'm sure he'll—

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:47.600
You're just a kid throwing a tantrum!

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:07.290
Kio!

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.870
Die, Gundam!

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:25.350
Snap out of it!

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:26.060
Do you want to die?

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:27.520
Ms. Shanalua!

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:29.520
Out of the way, small fry!

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:31.770
I'm here for the Gundam!

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:44.830
Die, Earther!

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:55.290
Ms. Shanalua!

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:11.020
Ms. Shanalua...

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:13.850
Kio...

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:17.070
